+// coop-pt1111b (Jep's 11-11 playtest, item 14: "P1 with a lightning weapon: P2 sometimes sees lightning particles on her screen
+// when P1 hits things, even far away"): whether a point is in front of the view drawn now. MGRotTransPers projects a point behind
+// the camera as if it were 1 in front (its depth clamped), which puts it on the screen near the middle; retail drew a bolt's four
+// corners that way unchecked, which one player's view never showed (the player faces what the weapon hits), but another
+// player's view of the same hit, facing away from it, did.
+bool InFront(const float *position) {
+    sceVu0FVECTOR point;
+
+    sceVu0ApplyMatrix(point, mgRenderInfo.view_scaled, const_cast<float *>(position));
+    return point[2] >= 1.0f;
+}
